# Product evidence and analysis

This repository provides product collection, preparation, modeling and an evidence
explorer. Research subjects, source inventories, observations, results and release
receipts are retained in ignored local documentation. This README describes the
software and its interfaces; it is not an inventory of collected data.

## Setup

```sh
uv sync --locked
python3 -B scripts/fetch_contracts.py --all
python3 -B scripts/fetch_contracts.py --all --offline
```

Contract bodies are dataset assets. Git keeps immutable references and checksums;
loaders verify files before using the ignored local caches. See the
[dataset contract guide](docs/data/dataset-contracts.md).

## Workflow

1. Preserve source records and original artifacts with the
   [collection plugin](plugins/category-research/README.md).
2. Research a category from preserved evidence using the
   [schema skill](plugins/category-processing/skills/category-schema/SKILL.md).
3. Apply published contracts through the
   [processing plugin](plugins/category-processing/README.md).
4. Prepare immutable [Gold inputs](docs/data/chocolate-gold.md) for a selected
   dataset-owned model design, then validate the [model](docs/model/spec.md).
5. Build and run the [web application](apps/web/README.md) against its pinned
   snapshot and model artifacts.

Bronze preserves evidence. Silver owns source identity, standardization,
corrections and profiling. Gold owns study-specific targets, features and input
selection. Preserve separate seller rows and immutable snapshots throughout.

The existing canonical command entry points are:

```sh
uv run python scripts/build_chocolate_silver.py --archive-root /path/to/collections --output /path/to/silver --offline
uv run python scripts/build_chocolate_gold.py --silver-root /path/to/silver --output /path/to/gold --offline
```

Their historical names identify implementation entry points, not collection
status. Use each command's `--help` for supported options. Standalone cleanup,
deduplication and standardization commands remain compatibility tools.

## Documentation and checks

[Project overview](PROJECT.md), [feature specifications](docs/spec.md),
[documentation policy](docs/documentation-policy.md), and
[implementation status](docs/lifecycle/plan.md) describe maintained behavior.

```sh
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check .
python3 -B scripts/check_documentation.py
```

Keep research details under ignored `docs/private/` or `data/investigation/`.
Private documents are optional for a clean checkout. Do not force-add research
reports, source excerpts, category catalogs or schema bodies to Git.
